import{_ as a,o as i,c as t,a5 as s}from"./chunks/framework.BfQ7H7Qx.js";const k=JSON.parse('{"title":"Historical Runbook — ECR Deployment Evolution (2026-10-29 → 2026-11-13)","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"operations/history/2026-10-29-ecr-deploy.md","filePath":"operations/history/2026-10-29-ecr-deploy.md"}'),n={name:"operations/history/2026-10-29-ecr-deploy.md"};function o(r,e,d,l,h,p){return i(),t("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[s(`<h1 id="historical-runbook-—-ecr-deployment-evolution-2026-10-29-→-2026-11-13" tabindex="-1">Historical Runbook — ECR Deployment Evolution (2026-10-29 → 2026-11-13) <a class="header-anchor" href="#historical-runbook-—-ecr-deployment-evolution-2026-10-29-→-2026-11-13" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Historical Runbook — ECR Deployment Evolution (2026-10-29 → 2026-11-13)&quot;">​</a></h1><p>&gt; <a href="./../../">&lt;&lt; Knowledge Base Home</a> · <a href="./../README.html">Operations</a> · <a href="./../deployment-acct134.html">Current Prod Deployment</a> &gt; &gt; <strong>Historical Record:</strong> Superseded by the current 5-EC2 topology on AWS account <code>134875421878</code> documented in <a href="./../deployment-acct134.html">deployment-acct134.md</a>.</p><h2 id="target-topology-planned-2026-11-13-not-yet-applied" tabindex="-1">Target topology (planned 2026-11-13, not yet applied) <a class="header-anchor" href="#target-topology-planned-2026-11-13-not-yet-applied" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Target topology (planned 2026-11-13, not yet applied)&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Host</th><th>Type</th><th>Containers</th><th>Compose</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>brandhub-api-gateway, 172.31.27.199</td><td>t3.small (2 GiB)</td><td>Nginx, API Gateway</td><td><code>backend.compose.json</code></td></tr><tr><td>brandhub-core-services, 172.31.24.149</td><td>m7i-flex.large (8 GiB)</td><td>AI (8082), Business (8081), Publisher (8083), PostgreSQL, Redis, RabbitMQ, ChromaDB</td><td><code>service.compose.json</code></td></tr><tr><td>brandhub-crawl, 172.31.20.50</td><td>m7i-flex.large (8 GiB)</td><td>crawl-service (8084, private)</td><td><code>crawl.compose.yaml</code></td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only the gateway is public (80/443). Gateway reaches Business, Publisher and Redis. Crawl reaches AI 8082, RabbitMQ 5672 and Redis 6379 on core; AI reaches crawl 8084. Business calls AI on the shared Docker network.</p><p>Private IPs are pinned in <code>terraform.tfvars</code>. AI drops from a 5 GiB to a 3 GiB budget because the browser crawler no longer runs inside it. Cutover: apply Terraform, move the AI volumes/env from gateway to core, start crawl, then deploy the AI CI change that targets the core instance.</p><h2 id="previous-two-ec2-layout-2026-11-03-historical" tabindex="-1">Previous two-EC2 layout (2026-11-03, historical) <a class="header-anchor" href="#previous-two-ec2-layout-2026-11-03-historical" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Previous two-EC2 layout (2026-11-03, historical)&quot;">​</a></h2><h2 id="production-rebalance-applied-2026-11-03" tabindex="-1">Production rebalance (applied 2026-11-03) <a class="header-anchor" href="#production-rebalance-applied-2026-11-03" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Production rebalance (applied 2026-11-03)&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The checked-in Compose files describe the deployed topology below. The original deployment inventory further down is historical. See the <a href="./2026-11-03-rebalance-ai.html">migration runbook and verified result</a>.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Host</th><th>Containers</th><th>AI budget</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Backend / gateway, 172.31.27.199</td><td>Nginx, API Gateway, AI API/crawler/consumer</td><td>5 GiB RAM, 1.5 CPUs</td></tr><tr><td>Service, 172.31.24.149</td><td>Business, Publisher, PostgreSQL, Redis, RabbitMQ, ChromaDB</td><td>AI removed</td></tr></tbody></table><p>AI data and model cache use named volumes on backend. Its runtime env file moves to backend as well. Business calls <code>http://172.31.27.199:8082</code>; AI calls Redis, RabbitMQ and ChromaDB at <code>172.31.24.149</code>. Ports 8082, 5672 and 8000 bind only to private IPs and are restricted to the corresponding peer security group. Redis reuses the existing private 6379 binding/rule. Host aliases preserve existing <code>redis</code>/<code>rabbitmq</code>/<code>chromadb</code> names in credential-bearing URLs without copying credentials into Compose.</p><p>The local, ignored <code>terraform.tfvars</code> sets both root disks to 20 GiB: gateway grows from 10 GiB; service stays at its current 20 GiB. Copy this sizing into the environment-specific Terraform inputs when deploying elsewhere. EC2 types remain <code>m7i-flex.large</code>.</p><p>AI and gateway CI acquire the same host lock, <code>/var/lock/brandhub-backend-compose.lock</code>, before modifying the shared backend manifest. GitHub concurrency groups alone do not serialize deployments across repositories. Deploy the workflow changes together with the host migration; leave CI paused until cutover verification finishes.</p><p>The 5 GiB limit is an initial budget, not proof that crawl OOM is fixed. AI dependencies, Business connectivity, public HTTPS and an actual browser launch/render/close smoke passed after cutover; the new AI cgroup recorded no OOM or restarts during these checks. Validate an actual bounded crawl after session re-upload. Facebook/Threads sessions are missing, TikTok is not configured, and secret-file storage remains unconfigured; these are separate from the successfully verified service connections.</p><h2 id="original-deployment-baseline" tabindex="-1">Original deployment baseline <a class="header-anchor" href="#original-deployment-baseline" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Original deployment baseline&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Deployment on 2026-10-29 uses immutable ECR tag <code>deploy-20261029</code> in account 821014378805, region ap-southeast-1.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Host</th><th>Address</th><th>Containers</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Backend</td><td>13.213.39.126 / 172.31.27.199</td><td>Nginx, API Gateway</td></tr><tr><td>Service</td><td>13.213.70.48 / 172.31.24.149</td><td>Business, Publisher, AI, PostgreSQL, Redis, RabbitMQ, ChromaDB</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Public API: <a href="https://api.brandhub.id.vn" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://api.brandhub.id.vn</a>. Frontend origin: <a href="https://brandhub.id.vn" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://brandhub.id.vn</a>.</p><p>Each server runs from <code>/home/ec2-user/brandhub/ecr</code>. Backend uses <code>backend.compose.json</code>, service uses <code>service.compose.json</code>. JSON files are accepted by Docker Compose. Each host receives only its own Compose and env files.</p><h2 id="environment-and-storage" tabindex="-1">Environment and storage <a class="header-anchor" href="#environment-and-storage" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Environment and storage&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Private runtime environment files are in <code>env/</code> on each host, mode 0600; directories are 0700. Local deployment env/JWT material is retained outside tracked source under <code>keep-local-only/ecr-deploy-20261029/private/</code>. Do not commit or bake these files into images.</p><p>Backend needs <code>env/api-gateway.env</code>. For the Video Space edit chat it also sets <code>EDIT_VIDEO_URL=https://api.brandhub.id.vn</code>, <code>EDIT_VIDEO_PATH_PREFIX=/edit-video</code> (through Nginx, so the waker starts a sleeping edit server) and <code>EDIT_VIDEO_API_KEY</code> (the Edit_Video server key, also in SSM <code>/brandhub/edit-video/EDIT_API_KEY</code>). Without them the <code>/api/v1/edit-video</code> route answers errors. Service needs separate env files for business-service, publisher-service, ai-service, postgres, redis and rabbitmq (MongoDB Atlas and Neo4j AuraDB are hosted externally). Missing runtime env files intentionally prevent Compose startup.</p><p>PostgreSQL uses the complete exported schema at <code>init/schema.sql</code>. The SQL file must be readable by the container&#39;s postgres user (0644). Initialization runs only for an empty data volume. The database has schema only; old data was not restored after the explicitly authorized EC2 replacement. Never use <code>down -v</code> during application updates.</p><p>Gateway reaches Business (8081), Publisher (8083) and Redis (6379) through the service host&#39;s private IP. Terraform permits these ports only from the backend Security Group. Other infrastructure ports have no host bindings. Only backend ports 80 and 443 are public.</p><h2 id="updating-application-images" tabindex="-1">Updating application images <a class="header-anchor" href="#updating-application-images" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Updating application images&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Build linux/amd64 images locally or in CI, tag each with a new unique release/commit tag, then push to <code>821014378805.dkr.ecr.ap-southeast-1.amazonaws.com/brandhub/&lt;service&gt;</code>. ECR tags are immutable; never overwrite <code>deploy-20261029</code>.</p><p>Authenticate the build machine:</p><div class="language-powershell vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">powershell</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">aws ecr </span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">get-login</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">-</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">password </span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">--</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">region ap</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">-</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">southeast</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">-</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">1</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;"> |</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;"> docker login </span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">--</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">username AWS </span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">--</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">password</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">-</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">stdin </span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">821014378805.dkr.ecr.ap-southeast-1.amazonaws.com</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Update the image tag in the appropriate Compose file, copy that file to the matching host, then run on that host:</p><div class="language-bash vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">bash</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">cd</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> /home/ec2-user/brandhub/ecr</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0;">aws</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> ecr</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> get-login-password</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> --region</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> ap-southeast-1</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;"> |</span><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0;"> docker</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> login</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> --username</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> AWS</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> --password-stdin</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> 821014378805.dkr.ecr.ap-southeast-1.amazonaws.com</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0;">docker</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> compose</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> -f</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> service.compose.json</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> config</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> -q</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0;">docker</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> compose</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> -f</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> service.compose.json</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> pull</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0;">docker</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> compose</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> -f</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> service.compose.json</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> up</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> -d</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> --no-build</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> --wait</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> --wait-timeout</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> 240</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0;">docker</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> compose</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> -f</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> service.compose.json</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> ps</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Use <code>backend.compose.json</code> on backend. EC2 authenticates ECR through its instance role, not stored AWS credentials. Existing application S3 credentials remain in the corresponding application env files.</p><p>Rollback: set the application image back to its previous immutable tag and repeat pull/up. Database migrations require a separate compatibility and rollback plan.</p><h2 id="https-and-external-integrations" tabindex="-1">HTTPS and external integrations <a class="header-anchor" href="#https-and-external-integrations" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;HTTPS and external integrations&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Let&#39;s Encrypt files are under <code>letsencrypt/</code> on backend; renewal uses <code>acme-webroot/</code>. <code>brandhub-certificate-renew.timer</code> checks twice daily and reloads Nginx after successful renewal. Inspect with <code>systemctl list-timers brandhub-certificate-renew.timer</code> and <code>journalctl -u brandhub-certificate-renew.service</code>.</p><p>OAuth callbacks configured in runtime env:</p><ul><li>Google: <code>https://api.brandhub.id.vn/api/v1/auth/oauth/google/callback</code></li><li>Facebook: <code>https://api.brandhub.id.vn/api/v1/social/facebook/callback</code></li><li>Instagram: <code>https://api.brandhub.id.vn/api/v1/social/instagram/callback</code></li><li>TikTok: <code>https://api.brandhub.id.vn/api/v1/social/tiktok/callback</code></li><li>Threads: <code>https://api.brandhub.id.vn/api/v1/social/threads/callback</code></li></ul><p>These same callback URLs must be registered in the respective provider consoles. Frontend must be built with <code>VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.brandhub.id.vn</code>; this deployment does not rebuild the S3/CloudFront frontend. Provider keys absent from the supplied env (e.g. image/video generation keys) remain unconfigured.</p><p>Infrastructure resources and DNS are managed in <code>brandhub-deloy/terraform/ec2-prod</code>. Update both runtime endpoints and DNS if replacing EC2 again, since private/public addresses are currently tied to these instances.</p><h2 id="deployment-verification-2026-10-29" tabindex="-1">Deployment verification (2026-10-29) <a class="header-anchor" href="#deployment-verification-2026-10-29" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Deployment verification (2026-10-29)&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>All four custom application images were built for linux/amd64, pushed to ECR and pulled on EC2. AI module import passed inside the image.</li><li>All application and database/cache/broker containers report healthy. AI health reports Redis, RabbitMQ and S3 clients connected; this is not an end-to-end check of paid providers or S3 operations.</li><li>Public HTTPS health returns <code>{&quot;status&quot;:&quot;UP&quot;}</code>. HTTP redirects to HTTPS (308).</li><li>CORS preflight from <code>https://brandhub.id.vn</code> returns 200 and the matching allowed origin.</li><li>Login with an empty JSON body reaches Business through Nginx/Gateway and returns the expected validation response (400). Protected unauthenticated endpoint returns 401.</li><li>Let&#39;s Encrypt renewal dry-run succeeded. Renewal timer is active.</li><li>Runtime env files are mode 0600. Compose manifests passed a scan against the supplied secret values.</li><li>Final Terraform plan reports no changes. No existing EC2 was destroyed during this deployment.</li></ul>`,40)])])}const u=a(n,[["render",o]]);export{k as __pageData,u as default};
